Analysis: Sigmund Freud proposed that child development proceeds through five stages of psychosexual development:
1. Oral stage (birth to 1 year) - focus on mouth and sucking (A);
2. Anal stage (1 to 3 years) - focus on bowel and bladder control (B);
3. Phallic stage (3 to 6 years) - focus on genitals, Oedipus/Electra complex (D);
4. Latency stage (6 years to puberty) - sexual impulses repressed, focus on school/social skills (E);
5. Genital stage (puberty onward) - mature adult sexuality and attachments (C).
Thus, the correct developmental sequence is (A), (B), (D), (E), (C).

